WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.750
(pleasant music)

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.750
- Meredith, how are you doing really?

00:00:14.211 --> 00:00:17.280
(Meredith sighs)

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.113
- Conflicted.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.140
There's been a lot of
stuff going on lately,

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.803
whether it's career stuff,

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.830
lots of frustration around that,

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:30.100
you know, being an employee
where you don't feel

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.660
as valued being on the front lines.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:34.080
So it's kinda hard to deal with.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.900
And I've been in contact with my dad

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.740
who I considered dead
to me three years ago,

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:41.713
and it's been a lot.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:46.890
So how am I?

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:51.280
I'm okay sometimes, but I
could use a good cry or two.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.650
- Yeah.

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:56.520
What causes you guys to reconnect?

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.570
- He went to rehab and,

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:01.980
'cause he was on meth,
doing a lot of drugs.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:04.840
And his ex told us that
he had been doing that,

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:06.520
he'd been getting better.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:10.480
And when they last spoke, he
said that my dad told him,

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:14.163
he knew he could have been a
better father to us growing up.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.140
And it just...

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.360
I needed to hear that.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:21.193
- Yeah.

00:01:21.193 --> 00:01:24.300
- He doesn't apologize, but in that way,

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.593
that was him apologizing.

00:01:28.944 --> 00:01:31.380
- I'm glad to hear that you
got to hear that from him

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:32.533
after all these years.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:36.100
- Yeah, not many people get closure,

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:36.933
but--
- Yeah.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.480
- Thank you for listening.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.340
- Yeah. Thank you for sharing.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:44.440
- What's in your mind?

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:46.800
- Right now?

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.870
I've been recently unemployed,

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:52.403
so I'm a little overwhelmed
with what I'm gonna do next.

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:54.820
- You know, it's funny
that you should say that,

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.860
'cause I feel the same way.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.860
I still have no idea what I wanna do.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:00.460
I'm happy that I have a job,

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:01.927
but it's not something that I wanna do,

00:02:01.927 --> 00:02:06.360
you know, I still gotta
find my passion, my truth.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:10.420
- There's a little, I
guess, comfort to know that

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.222
I'm not the only one going through it.

00:02:12.222 --> 00:02:13.055
- Yeah.

00:02:13.055 --> 00:02:15.100
- I mean, I'm sad that
we're all going through it.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.443
Makes me feel less lonely, I guess.

00:02:17.443 --> 00:02:18.276
How old are you?

00:02:18.276 --> 00:02:19.203
- I'm 31.

00:02:19.203 --> 00:02:20.036
How old are you?

00:02:20.036 --> 00:02:22.430
- I am about to be 30, I'm 29.

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:24.450
I mean, we're both still young.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:25.710
- Yeah, I know.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:27.540
Hopefully we'll get there.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.480
But, you know, be positive
and all that, you know,

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:31.830
can only, once again, take you so far,

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.420
but we gotta do what we gotta do.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.580
- Yeah.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:37.853
- What is the most romantic
thing that's happened to you?

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:40.540
- The most romantic?

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:42.423
I think I can think of one.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:46.830
I actually got picked up from therapy.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.123
Super romantic.

00:02:49.291 --> 00:02:51.960
Had bawled my eyes out for like an hour

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:56.340
and got picked up with
some of my favorite food.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:59.630
And we went to like a park at the beach

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:01.580
that I had never been to.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:04.090
And we just ate and played catch

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:06.473
with this thing called an Aerobie.

00:03:06.473 --> 00:03:07.730
I was freezing.

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:11.490
And usually, I can't deal
with the cold very well.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.083
But I remember just
thinking to myself how,

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:16.610
like the cold didn't bother me.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:17.773
So I think maybe that,

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:20.613
maybe that time.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.510
- And you said therapy?

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:25.490
- Yeah.

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:27.270
Do you go to therapy?

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:28.103
- I used to.

00:03:28.103 --> 00:03:30.570
I mean, I use it when I know I need it.

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:34.510
- Yeah.
- Yeah, my mental health stuff

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:38.550
started coming up since
I was like 12 or 13.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.313
So, been there, done that.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:44.870
Do you mind me asking like,
do you have any diagnosises?

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:48.243
Or is it just for talking to someone?

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:50.760
- I've struggled with depression

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:54.380
since I was super young, like eight.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.073
So I guess that would be
my official diagnosis.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:03:59.610
- Okay.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:02.070
Are you on antidepressants or anything?

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:03.530
- No, I haven't been for a while.

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:06.530
I haven't enjoyed the ones that I took

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:08.020
for how they make me feel.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:10.760
So, been trying to do it other ways,

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:14.210
doing it naturopathically
or with exercise and sleep

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:15.950
and just taking care of myself.

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:17.460
- Good for you.

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:18.670
Good for you.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:19.520
- What about you?

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:21.403
- Oh, yeah.

00:04:21.403 --> 00:04:22.380
- Wanna answer both questions?

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.670
- I forgot the list.

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:25.977
I forgot what the original question was.

00:04:25.977 --> 00:04:28.960
- But you wanna answer the
mental health question first?

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:30.580
- Oh, God, where do I start?

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:35.220
Major depressive disorder, anxiety, PTSD.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:37.293
Anxiety is getting better, thankfully.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.073
Now my doctors are on the track of ADHD.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.570
I've got diabetes, Hashimoto's.

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:47.330
My health is all like, all over the place.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:50.160
If it weren't for some of my meds,

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:55.160
I'd be practically a
puddle of mush, again.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:58.980
I couldn't function for a long time, so.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:01.470
- I'm glad to hear that
they're working for you.

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:02.303
- Thank you, thank you.

00:05:02.303 --> 00:05:04.400
- That's a big blessing, I'm sure.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.420
- Yeah, I felt like I
lost six years of my life.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:10.320
But now it's definitely catching up.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:11.538
I'm enjoying it.

00:05:11.538 --> 00:05:12.371
- That's great.

00:05:12.371 --> 00:05:13.580
The other question I think was

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:16.250
whenever you felt most
romanced in your life?

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.083
- Oh.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.720
And I'm sorry, I love you.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:22.990
That's my, my fiance's over (laughs)

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:24.160
We've all dated.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:26.940
Okay, one that comes to mind.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:31.570
First date, I meet this
guy at a coffee shop,

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:36.090
and after that, he takes me to his plane.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:38.320
And yes, I said his plane.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:43.320
And he flew us from
Albuquerque to Santa Fe.

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:45.700
- Wow.
- And from Santa Fe,

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:48.600
I was able, he taught
me how to fly a plane.

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:50.400
And it's like, you know, one
of those like little ones,

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.240
you can only seat like two people.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:55.690
But not every day you
get to say, oh, yeah,

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:59.540
yeah, he took me on a plane
and taught me how to fly it.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:00.400
- That's pretty awesome.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.020
- Yeah.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:04.820
- What's the most romantic
thing that's happened to you?

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.610
- The most romantic thing.

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:09.310
It is hard 'cause...

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:12.900
I need shots for this.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:18.740
I was engaged eight months
ago, so that thing, that ended,

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:20.550
you know, but I met her four years ago.

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:24.720
We were going to Catalina
Island, and we took a ferry,

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:25.810
and it was me, my brother,

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:27.785
and then this girl was
sitting with her friends,

00:06:27.785 --> 00:06:29.790
you know, it was like
a bachelorette party.

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:31.920
And she was just sitting, you
know, right across from me,

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:33.450
and I caught her looking at me.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:36.320
And I grew up in Boston and
Boston people are kinda forward.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:37.890
So I look at her, I was like,
"What are you looking at?"

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:39.363
In a, I guess, fun way.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.620
And she was like, "Oh, you
have, you know, nice skin."

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:44.097
I was like, "Oh, that's
creepy, but thank you.

00:06:44.097 --> 00:06:45.160
"I appreciate that."

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:48.380
So she laugh, I laugh, and
then after the boat stopped,

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:50.000
we walked towards the island,

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.810
and it was very, like, platonic
conversation, you know,

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:54.870
and I get to know her a little bit.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:56.600
And then in the end where it was like,

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.730
there was like two ways separating,

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:00.290
so she went with her friends

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:02.980
and then I went with my brother
and our friend, my friends,

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:03.850
and, you know, I told her like

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:05.070
it was really nice meet her

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:07.360
and hopefully, you know,
we'll come across again.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.430
And a couple of time has passed,

00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:10.520
and then I was with my brother,

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:14.290
we got another group
talking, and then I saw her,

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:15.750
and then I right away, ran up to her,

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:17.040
start talking to her.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:20.490
And something told me
that I had to kiss her.

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:22.430
I was like, "Hey, I have to kiss you."

00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:24.100
She's like, "What? Get
away from me, you creep."

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:25.950
In a fun way, I guess, right?

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:27.137
Like, "I'm sorry, I have to kiss you.

00:07:27.137 --> 00:07:28.570
"Something's telling me."

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:29.870
So she's like, fine.

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:33.440
So I kiss her, it was like
a really good novella kiss.

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:34.273
You know what I mean?

00:07:34.273 --> 00:07:35.890
Like, that good, the leg goes up.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.870
After that, the whole trip, it
was just me and her flirting.

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:40.550
And then she went back
home to Philadelphia,

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:42.020
I went back to San Diego.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:44.160
So she moved here, we started hanging out

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:45.450
and then one thing led to another

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:46.900
and then we started living together

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:50.740
and then I asked her to marry me,

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:52.680
you know, we were in Greece.

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:56.650
But the things with me is I
like to make people happy,

00:07:56.650 --> 00:07:58.360
regardless of what I want.

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:00.330
Strangers, friends, family, just,

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:02.240
I don't care, just as
long as you're happy.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:04.980
So the idea of marriage was her idea.

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:08.160
And then that idea became
kind of big in my mind now.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:09.940
I was like, I don't know
if I wanna marry her,

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:13.380
which it sucks 'cause she's
like six years older than me.

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:14.470
- Oh, she's ready to settle.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.280
- And then she's like,
"This is the ring I want."

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:17.700
I'm like, "Sure, absolutely."

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.629
And then something just hit like,

00:08:19.629 --> 00:08:21.210
I don't know if I wanna marry her.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:22.820
Which it sucks, which broke my heart,

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:25.080
because I felt like I wasted her time.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:29.040
And I wanted to be with
her, but something happened.

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:30.550
Like why'd this happen?

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:31.383
You know what I mean?

00:08:31.383 --> 00:08:32.216
Like, who's laughing at this?

00:08:32.216 --> 00:08:33.220
It's not funny.

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:36.230
So, I still feel guilty, you know?

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:38.980
But, then I did the whole move out

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:42.988
and all the fun thing,
cry a lot, you know?

00:08:42.988 --> 00:08:43.900
The youzsh.

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:45.650
- Well, I'm sorry that happened.

00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:46.483
- I know.

00:08:46.483 --> 00:08:47.316
Teachy moment.

00:08:47.316 --> 00:08:49.453
What about you? Any fun, sad story?

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.260
- Fun, sad story.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:55.480
I can't really think of
the last romantic thing

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:56.470
that's happened to me.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:09:01.470
I'm very torn between
liking romance and not.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:06.240
I feel like that I like the idea of it,

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:08.320
but when it's done to me,

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:10.290
it just doesn't feel very natural.

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:12.767
Maybe because it doesn't
come from the right person.

00:09:12.767 --> 00:09:13.600
- Yeah.

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:14.433
- It's happened a couple of times,

00:09:14.433 --> 00:09:15.900
but it just, it makes me uncomfortable,

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:18.000
because it's not from the person

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:18.980
I would want it to be from.

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:20.690
- Oh, I see.

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:21.809
Do you have somebody in mind?

00:09:21.809 --> 00:09:24.590
And then why don't you
just ask him out and

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:26.700
- No, I don't.
- do your own romantic thing?

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:28.100
I mean, it's the 21st century, girl,

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.870
you know what I mean?

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:31.010
Well, let me ask you,

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:33.410
do guys come up to you
and start talking to you?

00:09:35.579 --> 00:09:37.320
- Not a lot.

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:41.440
Maybe, I just don't come off too friendly.

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:42.930
- But guys still approach you, right?

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:43.977
Do you, in your mind, do you think like,

00:09:43.977 --> 00:09:45.750
"Okay, here comes another creep"?

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:47.210
- I think it's more the environment.

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:48.240
It depends on where I'm at.

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:50.450
If I'm in a club, and
everyone's kind of drunk,

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:52.380
I'm just like, I don't really.

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:55.140
If it was like a, you know, a more...

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:55.980
- Supermarket.

00:09:55.980 --> 00:09:57.990
- A supermarket or library, at a--

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.670
- Balboa Park, doing random interview.

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:00.595
You know what I mean?
- Yeah.

00:10:00.595 --> 00:10:02.583
- Stuff like that.

00:10:02.583 --> 00:10:03.640
- It'd be different.

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:04.473
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:10:04.473 --> 00:10:06.960
- What do your hands say about you?

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:07.900
- My hands?

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:08.830
- Yeah (chuckles)

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.350
(Meredith giggles)

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:13.570
- Currently, I have a
gorgeous engagement ring.

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:14.698
- Oh, congratulations.

00:10:14.698 --> 00:10:15.810
- Thank you.

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:18.230
He's the most incredible man ever.

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:20.500
I also, you can tell about me,

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:23.630
that, I don't know what you would call it,

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:25.520
brave or something, maybe?

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.760
I have some little hand tattoos.

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:30.870
One of them, it's a quote
on the side of my hand,

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:34.500
it says "Still I rise",
and I ended up getting it

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:37.640
because I've always loved
the poem from Maya Angelou.

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:41.960
But in symbolism with it
is that I'm a diabetic

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:44.850
and I've almost died like several times

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:46.990
for my sugars being too low.

00:10:46.990 --> 00:10:51.700
And so, anytime I got to
that, I was able to rise.

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:52.880
So, still I rise.

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:56.570
My blood sugars and just
out of that state, you know?

00:10:56.570 --> 00:10:57.820
In life.
- That's amazing.

00:10:57.820 --> 00:10:58.920
- Thank you.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.820
Something I wrote a while back,

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:02.390
now that I'm thinking about it,

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:05.070
it's, you can think of
hands in a different way,

